{% import "notes.html.j2" as notes %}
{#- Sub-agent activity: the text half of the swimlanes section (the
    chart itself is `charts.swimlanes`, embedded in the same section by
    the orchestrator). `subagent_notes` renders above the chart - how to
    read it, its per-label legend, and the honest classification state.
    Carries no <h3> - the section's own Jinja header (notes.section)
    names it. `state` is one of "not_run" / "warn" / "ok", the three
    honestly-distinguished classification states (see
    sections.subagent_notes).

    `has_end_markers` gates the how-to-read line entirely (there is no
    `{% raw %}{% else %}{% endraw %}` branch): everything that line
    explains - proportional box width, the completion glyph - exists
    only in that mode. Without recorded span ends the chart draws a thin
    colored tick at each span's start turn and this section renders no
    how-to-read line at all. The glyph is passed in as
    `end_marker_glyph` rather than typed here, so this line cannot name
    a character `charts._END_MARKER_SYMBOL` does not draw. -#}

{% macro subagent_notes(state, summary, has_end_markers, end_marker_glyph) -%}
{% if state == "not_run" %}<p class="meta">No sub-agent classification in this scan; lanes are shown without classification labels, as one neutral sub-agents group.</p>{% elif state == "warn" %}<p class="warning">&#9888; sub-agent classification rows exist in this scan but none joined this transcript's lanes (identity or span-id mismatch); all lanes shown unclassified.</p>{% endif %}{% if summary %}<p class="meta">{{ summary.n_spans }} sub-agent span(s) · {{ summary.judge_label }}: {{ summary.judges }}{% if summary.cohort %} · cohort: {{ summary.cohort.regime }} · mean span agreement: {{ summary.cohort.mean }} over {{ summary.cohort.n_spans }} span(s) with ≥ 2 voters{% endif %}{% if summary.verifier %} · verifier: {{ summary.verifier }}{% endif %}</p>{% endif %}{% if has_end_markers %}<p class="meta explainer">Spans sharing a row are different sub-agents packed to save vertical space (row count = peak concurrency). Box width is the span's first–last observed activity; {{ end_marker_glyph }} marks a recorded span completion.</p>{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- Each sub-agent's own spawn prompt, turn-ordered, in the same
    <details class="event event-list"> treatment as the flush/
    intervention lists - but each spawn is its own collapsed <details>:
    a one-line clamped summary (turn · label · preview), the full task
    text on open (scrolling past a cap), so a many-spawn run stays
    scannable instead of one text blob. `row.truncated` is set only on
    the fallback copy the judge saw. `row.text` is untrusted agent/user content, so it is
    interpolated raw exactly like phase_cards.html.j2's excerpt text
    - autoescape does the escaping. -#}
{% macro spawn_prompts(rows) -%}
<details class="event event-list"><summary>{{ rows|length }} sub-agent spawn(s)</summary>{% for row in rows %}<details class="spawn-item"><summary>turn {{ row.turn }}{% if row.label %} · {{ row.label }}{% endif %} · &ldquo;{{ row.text[:160] }}{% if row.text|length > 160 %}…{% endif %}&rdquo;</summary><p class="prompt-verbatim">{{ row.text }}{% if row.truncated %}…{% endif %}</p></details>{% endfor %}</details>
{%- endmacro %}
